      "id": "claim_66e450927755467baaa79fa2da438319",
      "statement": "The TypeScript package has a curated root rather than an aggregate of every feature: it exports the handwritten client and its public configuration/interface types, selected schemas, run-tree and utility APIs, prompt-cache APIs, generated error classes, and metadata constants, while broader capabilities use explicit subpaths. `js/scripts/create-entrypoints.js` owns those subpaths, generates ESM, CommonJS, and declaration forwarding shims, and rewrites the manifest's `exports` and `files`; the resulting manifest provides separate import, require, and type targets plus browser substitutions for internal filesystem and worker-thread utilities.",
